# Documentation sync (homecloud-docs)

**Mandatory:** when you add or change **user-facing** SDK behavior, update the docs site in the **same task** — never defer.

**Live site:** https://docs.web.holab.abrdns.com  
**Docs repo:** sibling `homecloud-docs/` (MkDocs; auto-deploys on push to `main`)

## This repo → docs

| Change | Update docs under |
|--------|-------------------|
| Public API (Python / JS) | `docs/en/sdk/` (+ HE when present) |
| Breaking API / env / behavior | New or updated page + `mkdocs.yml` nav if needed |

## Conventions

- **SO** not "storage" — URIs: `so://bucket/key`
- **MQ**, **MDB**, **Secrets** — use service short names consistently
- Code blocks, commands, JSON: always **LTR**

## Workflow

1. Implement here
2. Edit `homecloud-docs/docs/en/sdk/...` (and HE when present)
3. Run `mkdocs build --strict` in `homecloud-docs/`
4. Ship docs with the code when the user asks to push
5. Mention the docs update in your summary

## Do not

- Ship SDK changes without updating docs
- Say "docs can be updated later"
- Use `s3://` in new docs (docs use `so://`)
